# Force git to treat known text-source paths as TEXT for diff purposes —
# `diff` (bare, boolean-set) per gitattributes(5) §"Generating diff text":
# "A path to which the diff attribute is set is treated as text, even when
# they contain byte values that normally never appear in text files, such
# as NUL." Without this, git's content-sniffing heuristic (binary iff a NUL
# appears in the first core.bigFileThreshold-ish window, or the file looks
# sufficiently non-text) can render a path as `Bin N -> M bytes` with NO
# diff at all — unreviewable, in a repo whose entire review discipline is
# diff-based.
#
# This is DEFENSE IN DEPTH, not a substitute for
# `scripts/check-no-nul-bytes.ts` (the PREVENTIVE guard — fails the test
# suite outright when a raw NUL lands in a tracked text file; see its
# module header for the full mechanism and
# `task-literal-nul-bytes-in-two-scripts-source-files-one-is` for the
# incident). Two reasons this ALSO exists, not just the guard:
#
#   1. A `git commit --no-verify`/direct push bypasses any pre-commit or
#      pre-push wiring; this attribute keeps history reviewable regardless.
#   2. It is the ONLY fix for content ALREADY MERGED before the guard
#      existed: `scripts/migrate-test-budget-ledger-to-title-fingerprint.ts`
#      was committed with 4 raw NUL bytes (task
#      `task-literal-nul-bytes-in-two-scripts-source-files-one-is`) — even
#      after that content is fixed, `git diff`/`git show --stat` against the
#      PARENT commit still reports `Bin N -> M bytes`, because git's binary
#      check runs independently on EACH side of a diff and the parent's
#      blob is still genuinely NUL-poisoned. No amount of content-only
#      fixing in a later commit can retroactively un-poison a historical
#      blob; this attribute is what makes that specific diff (and any other
#      diff against a historically-poisoned blob) render as text anyway.
#      (Measured: `git diff --numstat`/`-a`/`--text` all still printed the
#      binary marker for that file WITHOUT this attribute; only the `diff`
#      gitattribute — not `text`, which governs line-ending conversion, a
#      different concern — fixed the numstat line.)
#
# This list mirrors `scripts/check-no-nul-bytes.ts`'s
# TEXT_SOURCE_EXTENSIONS/TEXT_SOURCE_DOTFILES allowlist — the same
# classification of "this is a file we hand-author as text" governs both
# "must never contain a raw NUL" (the guard) and "must always diff as text
# regardless" (this file). Keep the two lists in sync.
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
*.js diff
*.jsx diff
*.mjs diff
*.cjs diff
*.mts diff
*.cts diff
*.json diff
*.md diff
*.mdx diff
*.yaml diff
*.yml diff
*.sh diff
*.css diff
*.html diff
*.txt diff
*.toml diff
*.sql diff
*.py diff
*.template diff
*.example diff
*.lock diff
.gitignore diff

# Extensionless shebang scripts (no glob covers these; list explicitly —
# see check-no-nul-bytes.ts's hasShebang/hasNoExtension for the same pair).
hooks/pre-push diff
assets/project/pre-push diff
